{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02098",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.96,
      "end_seconds": 8.07,
      "duration_seconds": 7.11,
      "text": "Right, hi, doctor, I came as soon as they called me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.21,
      "end_seconds": 14.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "You're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.17,
      "end_seconds": 26.19,
      "duration_seconds": 10.02,
      "text": "Mainly a shaky feeling in my hands. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.43,
      "end_seconds": 32.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.86,
      "end_seconds": 55.96,
      "duration_seconds": 19.1,
      "text": "Ah, I'd say moderate. Yes, caffeine. That makes it worse. My neighbour said I should get it looked at. I did have butterflies in my stomach at one point, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.65,
      "end_seconds": 64.74,
      "duration_seconds": 8.09,
      "text": "So, have you had a shaky feeling in your hands before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.58,
      "end_seconds": 70.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "A bit, last year. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.17,
      "end_seconds": 74.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Right, has there been any weakness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.79,
      "end_seconds": 78.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Definitely no weakness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.3,
      "end_seconds": 83.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Did you get palpitations, weight loss or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.29,
      "end_seconds": 88.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Um, no, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.47,
      "end_seconds": 92.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "How are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.78,
      "end_seconds": 96.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "I move fine otherwise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.68,
      "end_seconds": 106.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "Anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.01,
      "end_seconds": 115.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "My heart's been fine, as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.75,
      "end_seconds": 121.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.07,
      "end_seconds": 131.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Mm, my father has Parkinson's disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.22,
      "end_seconds": 137.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.69,
      "end_seconds": 153.23,
      "duration_seconds": 13.54,
      "text": "I've never touched a cigarette. I look after my grandchildren most days. No, I share a house with my brother. I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.31,
      "end_seconds": 157.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.44,
      "end_seconds": 164.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "Yes, thin bones. Heart failure, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.54,
      "end_seconds": 166.35,
      "duration_seconds": 0.81,
      "text": "Mm-hmm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.09,
      "end_seconds": 168.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "Yes, depression."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.04,
      "end_seconds": 173.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "Okay, I can see heart failure in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.15,
      "end_seconds": 189.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.05,
      "end_seconds": 197.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Alendronate, 70 milligrams, once a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.2,
      "end_seconds": 201.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Roughly how long on that one?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.7,
      "end_seconds": 204.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "About a year now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.36,
      "end_seconds": 206.06,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.22,
      "end_seconds": 216.75,
      "duration_seconds": 6.53,
      "text": "I'm on metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day for my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.81,
      "end_seconds": 220.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.58,
      "end_seconds": 228.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "For two years. Escitalopram. I take it 10 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.75,
      "end_seconds": 230.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Okay, go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.75,
      "end_seconds": 246.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.29,
      "end_seconds": 254.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.96,
      "end_seconds": 278.24,
      "duration_seconds": 6.28,
      "text": "Okay: temperature 36.6, pulse 83. And BP is 123 over 70, respiratory rate 18."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.75,
      "end_seconds": 282.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.64,
      "end_seconds": 285.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "That's fine, I'll explain it soon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.71,
      "end_seconds": 290.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.17,
      "end_seconds": 293.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.77,
      "end_seconds": 315.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.14,
      "text": "There is a fine, fast tremor that goes away when the hands are resting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 317.16,
      "end_seconds": 318.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.83,
      "end_seconds": 325.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "You can relax now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.27,
      "end_seconds": 369.37,
      "duration_seconds": 28.1,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, it fits best with an anxiety or caffeine-related tremor. I think a thyroid test makes sense here, for tremor. Cut down caffeine and try slow breathing when it starts. If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. Right, is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 370.43,
      "end_seconds": 374.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.7,
      "end_seconds": 376.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "Goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}